@extends('layouts.app')

@section('content')
<div class="container docs-shell">
    @include('partials.docs-side')
    <article class="docs-body">
        <h1>Installation</h1>
        <p>Kotlimo is an open-source Kotlin web framework. Clone the repository, run the tests, then either serve this documentation site or scaffold a new app.</p>

        <h2>Requirements</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>JDK 21 or newer</li>
            <li>The Gradle wrapper in this repository (<code class="inline">./gradlew</code>)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Clone and test</h2>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/kotlimo/kotlimo.git
cd kotlimo
./gradlew test
./gradlew :website:run</code></pre>
        <p>The development server starts at <code class="inline">http://127.0.0.1:8000</code>. This documentation site is the <code class="inline">website/</code> module — a Kotlimo application.</p>

        <h2>Create an application</h2>
        <p>From a clone of this repository:</p>
        <pre><code>./gradlew :kotlimo-console:run --args='new blog'
# equivalent:
./kotlimo new blog
cd blog
./gradlew run</code></pre>
        <p>The generator writes Gradle files, <code class="inline">config/*.json</code>, a HomeController, Kote views, <code class="inline">.env.example</code>, and a users-table migration. If it can see the Kotlimo source tree, it adds a Gradle composite <code class="inline">includeBuild</code> so you do not need published JARs.</p>

        <h2>Depend on Kotlimo from another project</h2>
        <p>Modules publish as <code class="inline">io.kotlimo:kotlimo-*</code> version <code class="inline">0.1.0</code>. The usual dependency is the foundation module, which pulls HTTP, views, and the database layer:</p>
        <pre><code>dependencies {
    implementation("io.kotlimo:kotlimo-foundation:0.1.0")
}</code></pre>
        <p>While you are hacking on the framework, include the clone as a composite build (the <code class="inline">new</code> command does this for you):</p>
        <pre><code>// settings.gradle.kts
includeBuild("/path/to/kotlimo")</code></pre>
        <p>To consume GitHub Packages instead, publish from this repo and authenticate:</p>
        <pre><code>./gradlew publish   # needs GITHUB_ACTOR and GITHUB_TOKEN

maven {
    url = uri("https://maven.pkg.github.com/kotlimo/kotlimo")
    credentials {
        username = providers.environmentVariable("GITHUB_ACTOR").get()
        password = providers.environmentVariable("GITHUB_TOKEN").get()
    }
}</code></pre>

        <h2>Configuration</h2>
        <p>Copy <code class="inline">.env.example</code> to <code class="inline">.env</code>. Nested JSON under <code class="inline">config/</code> is loaded at boot. Environment variables overlay matching keys. See <a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a>.</p>
    </article>
</div>
@endsection
